In my current Ranger game I reached Medusa's level without any
convenient way to cross the water, so after taking out the local titan
with a single barrage of poisoned arrows, I decided to just dig down and
avoid Medusa for the time being.  Unfortunately, I landed right in the
lap of a master mind flayer; fortunately, my helmet blocked all but one
of its brain-sucking attacks.  I teleported a short distance away,
engraved the E word, and donned a ring of conflict until the local
monsters (of which there was a curious profusion) had mostly taken each
other out.

Exploring the level, I found that it contained *three* player graves:
"...killed by a master mind flayer," "...choked on a stone giant
corpse," and "...killed by a bolt of cold."  Aside from multiple
well-stocked bags of holding, the booty included the Heart of Ahriman,
Magicbane, Sunsword, Vorpal Sword, the Eye of the Aethiopica, and a
runesword that I suppose would have been Stormbringer if I weren't
already carrying it.  So much for my plan to get a second artifact from
the castle wand before finishing the Quest!

I'm going to feel dumb as hell if I can't win the game now.
Unfortunately, when I went back up to Medusa's level with a towel around
my head, I found myself adjacent to both Medusa and a nymph.  I beat a
hasty retreat, terrified that the nymph would steal some items and leave
my vulnerable to Medusa before I could take her out.


